@id n2_osric
# DRAFT
# Osric at the kitchen fire at dusk (night 2). Jolly; he carried the drowned merchant (he handles the bodies).
# He noticed whether the porter ate his bread last night (n1_ate_bread). Asking what's in the bread, once warned,
# is the wrong question to the wrong brother (Suspicion +5), and ends the talk on his question.
# Claims: n2_osric_rye (hiding: the rye is the abbey's own, and it carries the ergot the cult doses the house with).
== start
(Osric at the kitchen fire again, red-faced from it. He waves a ladle at you.)
-> dead [if died_merchant]
-> ate [if n1_ate_bread]
-> left

== dead
Osric {sad, smile}: A sad morning's work. I helped carry that merchant out of the pond, heavy as wet barley. Not kitchen talk.
-> ate [if n1_ate_bread]
-> left

== ate
Osric {glad}: You cleared your trencher last night! That's a porter I like.
-> topics

== left
Osric {glad}: You left your bread last night, brother. My bread! (He laughs, but his eyes stay on you.)
Osric {amused}: Tonight you'll eat it, or I'll know why.
-> topics

== again
Osric {glad}: Back for a taste? Not till the bell.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n2_osric_supper] What's for supper, brother? -> supper
* [if bread_warned] [if not n2_osric_bread] [if not read_n2_osric_rye] What's in the bread, brother? -> bread

== supper [set n2_osric_supper]
Osric {glad}: Eels, stewed, if the eelman got through the rain. He did. And the bread, with a heel put by for you.
-> topics

== bread [set n2_osric_bread] [suspicion 5]
-> n2_osric_rye

== n2_osric_rye [claim n2_osric_rye hiding]
Osric {glad, smile}: In my bread? Rye and salt and water and my own two hands. Rye from our own granary.
* [believe] Then I'll eat it, brother, and gladly. -> rye_believed
* [press] Nothing else in it, brother? Nothing at all? -> rye_pressed

== rye_believed
Osric {glad}: That's the porter I like. The heel's put by for you, mind.
(He goes back to his kneading.)
-> end

== rye_pressed
(He keeps smiling. He has stopped kneading.)
Osric {wary}: Who's been talking to you about my bread, brother?
-> end

== leave
Osric {glad}: Come hungry, mind!
